      <guid>http://localhost:1313/nearest-aircraft-display/</guid>
      <description>&lt;figure class=&#34;responsive-image&#34;&gt;&#xA;    &lt;img &#xA;      src=&#34;http://localhost:1313/nearest-aircraft-display/chatgpt-header-image_hu_5f0d7fa989fc2f5f.webp&#34;&#xA;      srcset=&#34;http://localhost:1313/nearest-aircraft-display/chatgpt-header-image_hu_153939f10a12373d.webp 320w, http://localhost:1313/nearest-aircraft-display/chatgpt-header-image_hu_d4c9a35156bde7dc.webp 480w, http://localhost:1313/nearest-aircraft-display/chatgpt-header-image_hu_59890c2ad19508e.webp 768w, http://localhost:1313/nearest-aircraft-display/chatgpt-header-image_hu_5f0d7fa989fc2f5f.webp 1024w, http://localhost:1313/nearest-aircraft-display/chatgpt-header-image_hu_77129e117855f9eb.webp 1366w, http://localhost:1313/nearest-aircraft-display/chatgpt-header-image_hu_8a5602adb3d2f838.webp 1536w, http://localhost:1313/nearest-aircraft-display/chatgpt-header-image_hu_7f0fb93a88b74818.webp 1920w, http://localhost:1313/nearest-aircraft-display/chatgpt-header-image_hu_2136d08c7aa574cb.webp 2560w, http://localhost:1313/nearest-aircraft-display/chatgpt-header-image_hu_20972247bce3265f.webp 3840w&#34;&#xA;      sizes=&#34;100vw&#34;&#xA;      width=&#34;100%&#34;&#xA;      style=&#34;max-width: 100%; height: auto; background-size: cover; background-image: url(data:image/webp;base64,UklGRgwBAABXRUJQVlA4IAABAABQBgCdASoqABoAPrlEmEUjoiEYBqg7C4TygFt9uTLei/e96t2&amp;#43;q5fcwJdIuf34j3Rt9uCsMLgN2snTAAD&amp;#43;83J6NAQyAToqF8VrR/hC2KdTPgL&amp;#43;pX5vR7p9VE02kQ4eGqEjEOlLRG5KR3yAwoEoU7JD6CdMg/Ya28zPeciIcAB43DQKxwHhAJgqsvUqRyVkxcXzAiy4iUGCwyKzJf2ULaFiFxD8x&amp;#43;hf4KMYeXI5jRpRoEh1w1FgMKNhjO7jBL0CrJQf9cYNx6K&amp;#43;Dby33ZFzHAHLLz9KQ25dOpMa7IYGjY/uiff&amp;#43;pHxIs4uuXcVfIWYvwSGUAOuf79DcTIdt/zYBwgAA);&#34;&#xA;      loading=&#34;lazy&#34;&#xA;      decoding=&#34;async&#34;&#xA;      alt=&#34;ChatGPT generated image of Flight Display&#34; /&gt;&#xA;    &#xA;    &#xA;    &#xA;    &#xA;  &lt;/figure&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;I have an &lt;a href=&#34;http://localhost:1313/piaware-lcd-display/&#34;&gt;ADS-B node&lt;/a&gt; feeding data into the vast network of flight trackers, but it mostly just sits on my roof humming along without any interaction from me. I can, and have, looked at the webpage that shows my local flight data and the planes on a map, but it didn’t quite have the whimsy I was after. I decided a wall-mounted device that displayed the aircraft type closest to my location at any given moment would be a fun build.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>PiAware Data Display</title>
      <link>http://localhost:1313/piaware-lcd-display/</link>
      <pubDate>Sat, 01 Mar 2025 19:05:55 -0700</pubDate>
      <guid>http://localhost:1313/piaware-lcd-display/</guid>
      <description>&lt;figure class=&#34;responsive-image&#34;&gt;&#xA;    &lt;img &#xA;      src=&#34;http://localhost:1313/piaware-lcd-display/piaware-lcd-chatgpt-generated_hu_cd0cba0d659be1e8.webp&#34;&#xA;      srcset=&#34;http://localhost:1313/piaware-lcd-display/piaware-lcd-chatgpt-generated_hu_ae8bf96b21d45ed9.webp 320w, http://localhost:1313/piaware-lcd-display/piaware-lcd-chatgpt-generated_hu_2cef0c1514f24b4.webp 480w, http://localhost:1313/piaware-lcd-display/piaware-lcd-chatgpt-generated_hu_9f6bc1f7d58d596a.webp 768w, http://localhost:1313/piaware-lcd-display/piaware-lcd-chatgpt-generated_hu_cd0cba0d659be1e8.webp 1024w, http://localhost:1313/piaware-lcd-display/piaware-lcd-chatgpt-generated_hu_cda584bca09e7262.webp 1366w, http://localhost:1313/piaware-lcd-display/piaware-lcd-chatgpt-generated_hu_b64117f354ce4cc8.webp 1536w, http://localhost:1313/piaware-lcd-display/piaware-lcd-chatgpt-generated_hu_3718102d5e11443f.webp 1920w, http://localhost:1313/piaware-lcd-display/piaware-lcd-chatgpt-generated_hu_221b2ef9c0957c34.webp 2560w, http://localhost:1313/piaware-lcd-display/piaware-lcd-chatgpt-generated_hu_275d735de4525e91.webp 3840w&#34;&#xA;      sizes=&#34;100vw&#34;&#xA;      width=&#34;100%&#34;&#xA;      style=&#34;max-width: 100%; height: auto; background-size: cover; background-image: url(data:image/webp;base64,UklGRu4AAABXRUJQVlA4IOIAAACwBQCdASoqABoAPs1MnkejoiEYCq1UOwzE8QAXd0BTK/nBU1ZqxbQba8RLQLoI0qA6bAnKAgAA/vfn&amp;#43;xphXcN6HQT9OhUYKo86MLbX/w7ubr4LpQvwZt30GSEgsPew&amp;#43;K7gCQMcpDRY3JAkiCt0i2aba29S2LItHW14yWebyVsvsufi0nm4k7IzfA0KlSDxU4ynpeZcNwS&amp;#43;wyO2b18mojNTqZaO21GjzNmTwehSygW0k90w8PEm4Hcp7SPVuSI5nv34K4dZr55x5d5Znhc&amp;#43;YZdU&amp;#43;N9hfQWce1ZOAonBoVFH3CAA);&#34;&#xA;      loading=&#34;lazy&#34;&#xA;      decoding=&#34;async&#34;&#xA;      alt=&#34;ChatGPT generated image of ADS-B Node&#34; /&gt;&#xA;    &#xA;    &#xA;    &#xA;    &#xA;  &lt;/figure&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;After setting up my PiAware receiver to track live flight data, I wanted a simple way to glance at some key stats without SSH-ing into the Pi or opening a browser. Enter the humble 20x4 I2C LCD screen.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;This post walks through how I wired up a character LCD to my Raspberry Pi, wrote some Python to pull flight data from PiAware, and got a tiny dashboard updating every second—all without needing to touch a GUI.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
